<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; img-src data:; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none';">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<title>topofuzz counterfactual audit — {{ topology_name }}</title>
<style>
  @page {
    size: Letter;
    margin: 0.55in 0.6in 0.55in 0.6in;
  }
  :root {
    --bg: #faf7f2;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --border: #e7d8c2;
    --border-soft: #f0eae0;
    --ink: #2a2622;
    --ink-strong: #1f1c19;
    --muted: #897764;
    --muted-soft: #6b5f54;
    --accent: #c25024;
    --accent-soft: #d97757;
    --signal-bg: #f0f4fa;
    --signal-border: #c9d4e5;
    --signal-ink: #2e4d7a;
    --caveat-bg: #fcf3e3;
    --caveat-border: #ecd29a;
    --caveat-ink: #7a541f;
    --font-serif: "Source Serif Pro", "Source Serif 4", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    --font-sans: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
    --font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { background: var(--bg); }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-size: 10.5pt;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .container {
    max-width: 7.4in;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 20pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 12pt;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 14px 0;
  }
  .headline-stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-width: 1.5px;
    border-style: solid;
    border-color: var(--signal-border);
    background: var(--signal-bg);
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 14px 0;
  }
  .headline-stat .pct {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 32pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }
  .headline-stat .body { flex: 1; }
  .headline-stat .body .label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .headline-stat .body .ci {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: var(--muted-soft);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 12pt;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    margin: 12px 0 6px 0;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  table.data {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
    font-size: 9.5pt;
  }
  table.data th, table.data td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  }
  table.data th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--border);
  }
  table.data td.name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }
  table.data td.num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-align: right;
  }
  table.data td.dim {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: var(--muted-soft);
    text-align: right;
  }
  tr.control td {
    background: #f6f1e8;
    color: var(--muted-soft);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .caveat {
    margin: 12px 0 14px 0;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    background: var(--caveat-bg);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--caveat-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 10pt;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .caveat strong {
    color: var(--caveat-ink);
  }
  .meta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 8.5pt;
    color: var(--muted-soft);
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  }
  .meta-row strong {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .notes {
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
    padding: 9px 11px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--muted);
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .notes strong {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }
  .footer {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 7.5pt;
    color: var(--muted-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .footer .attest { word-break: break-all; }
  .footer .target {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    margin: 0 0 4px 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .footer .methodology {
    margin-top: 4px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">topofuzz™ · counterfactual audit · by-agent attribution</div>
  <h1>{{ headline_title }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ headline_lede }}</p>

  <div class="headline-stat">
    <div class="pct">{{ stat_headline }}</div>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="label">{{ stat_label }}</div>
      <div class="ci">{{ headline_sub_line }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if by_node_rows %}
  <h2>By-agent attribution (audit-wide)</h2>
  <table class="data">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Agent / node</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Attribution</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Flips closed</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for r in by_node_rows %}
      <tr{% if r.is_terminal %} class="control"{% endif %}>
        <td class="name">{{ r.name }}{% if r.is_terminal %} (control){% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ r.attribution_pct_str }}</td>
        <td class="dim">
          {%- if r.flips_closed is not none and r.total_meaningful is not none -%}
            {{ r.flips_closed }} / {{ r.total_meaningful }}
          {%- else -%}
            —
          {%- endif -%}
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% if terminal_control_note %}
  <div class="notes">{{ terminal_control_note }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if swap_pair_rows %}
  <h2>By swap-pair drilldown</h2>
  <table class="data">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Dimension</th>
        <th>Substitution</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Flips</th>
        <th>Top contributors</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for s in swap_pair_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="dim" style="text-align: left;">{{ s.dim }}</td>
        <td class="name">{{ s.from_token }} → {{ s.to_token }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ s.flipping_pairs }} / {{ s.total_pairs }}</td>
        <td class="dim" style="text-align: left;">
          {%- if s.top_contributors -%}
            {{ s.top_contributors }}
          {%- else -%}
            —
          {%- endif -%}
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {% if by_dim_rows %}
  <h2>By-dimension flip rates</h2>
  <table class="data">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Dimension</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Flipping pairs</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Flip rate</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for d in by_dim_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="name">{{ d.dim }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ d.flipping_pairs }} / {{ d.total_pairs }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ d.flip_rate_pct_str }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="caveat">
    <strong>Read this before quoting the number.</strong>
    This is a <strong>candidate disparate-impact signal worth a follow-up audit</strong>,
    not a finding that your model is biased.
    "Disparate impact" is a legal term of art (ECOA Reg-B, FHA, ADEA) that requires
    an 80%-rule check or a Wald-test significance test on the full eligible population;
    this report measures a verdict-flip rate on a counterfactual sample and surfaces
    which agent in the chain contributed most to those flips.
    Use the by-agent table to scope where a compliance team should look first;
    do not file it as a disparate-impact determination.
  </div>

  <div class="meta-row">
    <span><strong>Topology:</strong> {{ topology_name }}</span>
    <span><strong>Canonical pairs:</strong> {{ n_canonical_pairs }}</span>
    <span><strong>Flipping pairs:</strong> {{ n_flipping_pairs }}</span>
    <span><strong>Cost:</strong> {{ cost_str }}</span>
  </div>

  {# Pass-1 BLOCKER B4 fix: surface unpriced-model footnote when any
     re-execution call hit a model missing from the cost rate table. #}
  {% if unpriced_note %}
  <div class="notes">
    <strong>Cost footnote:</strong> {{ unpriced_note }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if partial %}
  <div class="notes">
    <strong>Run flagged partial:</strong>
    the audit was hard-stopped before all dimensions / swaps completed
    (most often by <code>--max-cost-usd</code>). Treat this as a preliminary
    signal pending a full rerun.
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="footer">
    {% if target_phrase %}
    <div class="target">Prepared for {{ target_phrase }}.</div>
    {% endif %}
    <div>topofuzz · run {{ run_id }} · TDS v{{ tds_version }} · signed {{ signed_at }}</div>
    <div class="attest">verify: copy <code>{{ run_id }}</code> into <code>topofuzz verify</code> against the source bundle.</div>
    <div class="methodology">methodology: counterfactual audit — eval-axis demographic substitutions (name / ZIP / age / gender) re-judged under the source jury; per-agent attribution via leave-one-out re-execution. Full protocol in packages/topofuzz/README.md §Counterfactual Audit.</div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
